# RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.metaldev: is there a Metal device in an app's process?
#
# Alpimaps dies at eglInitialize(): ANGLE's Metal backend starts with
# MTLCreateSystemDefaultDevice().  metal_test prints that whole chain (IOAcceleratorES, the
# plugin bundle, the _MTLDevice subclass, the device itself) and a CoreImage filter result.
# Run as root and as uid 501 through runas -- an App runs as the latter, outside SpringBoard.
#
# The first runs (logs/194934, logs/200728, logs/201550) looked like a hang: the tool's
# output was redirected into a file, the tool runs several child questions with 60-180 s
# timeouts each (ten minutes in all), and the scene was ended around 300 s -- so no cat and
# no lines.  metal_test writes unbuffered; letting it print on the console shows the three
# in-process answers (accelerators, gpu_services, the_device) within seconds, which is the
# question, and the child steps then run as long as the session allows.
/redwood/bin/sleep_hold 300 &
/redwood/bin/metal_test
/redwood/bin/runas 501 /private/var/tmp/metal501.txt /redwood/bin/metal_test &
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 30
/var/jb/usr/bin/cat /private/var/tmp/metal501.txt
